 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518481,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Paola takes out a 75-day loan for $3,500.00. Her interest rate is 11.2%. If she makes a partial payment of $1,250.00 after 30 days, what will her payoff be at the end of the loan?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Interest on the loan after 75 days:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"I = P \\times r \\times t = 3,500 \\times 0.112 \\times \\frac{{75}}{{365}} \\approx \\$ 80.547\"></span></p>\n<p>Interest on the loan after 30 days:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"I = P \\times r \\times t = 3,500 \\times 0.112 \\times \\frac{{30}}{{365}} \\approx \\$ 32.22\"></span> (rounded to the nearest cent)</p>\n<p>Subtract the partial interest off the loan payment.</p>\n<p>$1,250 – 32.22 = $1,217.78 went toward paying off the loan.</p>\n<p>$3,500 – 1217.78 = $2,282.22 is the remaining balance of the loan.</p>\n<p>There are 45 more days to pay interest:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"I = P \\times r \\times t = 2282.22 \\times 0.112 \\times \\frac{{45}}{{365}} \\approx \\$ 31.52\"></span> more interest will accrue.</p>\n<p>The total payout left of the loan is the balance of the loan plus the additional interest.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2,282.22 + 31.52 = \\$2,313.74\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$2,313.74"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
